From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] misc: Add Oculus Quest 2 syncboss SPI link driver

The Oculus Quest 2 has an nRF52832 sensor-hub MCU ("syncboss") on SPI
that carries the IMU, magnetometer, controller and proximity data. This
is a rewrite of the transport part of the vendor's GPL-2.0 driver,
keeping its device names and record format (syncboss0,
syncboss_stream0, syncboss_control0).

It has no MCU programming path, and userspace can send only the IMU
start and stop commands, matched byte for byte against a table. On last
close the driver sends the vendor SHUTDOWN packet and holds the MCU in
reset. syncboss0 refuses to open if frames would use SE DMA and
quest2_syncboss.identity_dma=1 is not set.

The wire-format helpers have KUnit tests.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
